-- title:
--   Dual root of a complex number
-- statement:
--   For $z\in\mathbb C$, the dual root is
--   $$
--   \mathrm{dualRoot}(z)=\frac{\sqrt{|z|}\,\overline z}{|z|},
--   $$
--   interpreted as $0$ when $z=0$. It satisfies $z\cdot\mathrm{dualRoot}(z)=|z|^{3/2}$ and $|\mathrm{dualRoot}(z)|=|z|^{1/2}$, so $|\mathrm{dualRoot}(z)|^3=|z|^{3/2}$. This is the extremal dual element for the $L^{3/2}$–$L^3$ duality. It is used to linearize $\frac32$-moments of the maximal function into a trilinear pairing with a third function in $L^3$.
